Dear all,

This is Day 1 of a 7-day public record concerning Judicial Review AC-2025-L=
ON-004293. Each statement addresses a distinct matter formally raised and no=
t determined.

They include the removal of participation measures granted in recognition o=
f autism and PTSD, without any identified judicial order, hearing, or reason=
s; a criminal referral to the Metropolitan Police; and a sworn financial rep=
resentation that is contradicted by contemporaneous SEC filings and Nasdaq m=
arket information.

The financial disclosure relates to a SPAC controlled by Kenes Rakishev, a =
Kazakh businessman with documented links to Andrew Mountbatten-Windsor.

Since February 2024, these matters have been raised across court proceeding=
s, parliamentary submissions, and criminal referral channels. No institution=
 has substantively engaged. No determinations have been identified.

The attached statement provides a structured summary. A one-page overview o=
f the five core matters is also attached. A submission and response chronolo=
gy evidencing institutional handling across 61 formal submissions is include=
d.

A complete evidential record is available in the public archive: https://gi=
thub.com/nadiazahmoul/Zahmoul-v-SSJ-HMCTS-Public-Archive

Further material will follow, one issue per day.

Kind regards,=20

Nadia Zahmoul

